<title>BRAZIL: SOCCER-LIBERTADORES CUP RESULTS/STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-LIBERTADORES CUP RESULTS/STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-03-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of South American Libertadores Cup first round matches played Friday.</p>
<p>Group 1</p>
<p>In Asuncion: Cerro Porteno (Paraguay) 2 Oriente Petrolero (Bolivia) 1 (halftime 1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Cerro Porteno - Felix Britez 23, Justo Meza 90</p>
<p>Oriente Petrolero - Jorge Diduch 60</p>
<p>Group 2</p>
<p>In Buenos Aires: Racing Club (Argentina) 2 Nacional (Ecuador) 0 (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Sebastian Brusco 48, Ruben Capria 77</p>
<p>Group 4</p>
<p>In Porto Alegre, Brazil: Gremio (Brazil) 2 Alianza (Peru) 0 (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Emerson 59, Ze Alcino 80</p>
<p>    Standings		   Pl  W  D  L  F A  Pts</p>
<p>Group 1</p>
<p> Bolivar (Bolivia)	     4  3  1  0 14  5  10</p>
<p> Oriente Petrolero	     6  2  2  2  9 10   8</p>
<p> Guarani (Paraguay)	    5  1  2  2  5 10   5</p>
<p> Cerro Porteno		   5  1  1  3  5  8   4</p>
<p>(Bolivar, Oriente Petrolero already qualified)</p>
<p>Group 2</p>
<p> Velez Sarsfield (Argentina) 5  4  0  1  9  4  12</p>
<p> Nacional			  6  3  0  3  5  7   9</p>
<p> Emelec (Ecuador)		4  1  1  2  6  7   4</p>
<p> Racing Club		     5  1  1  3  5  7   4</p>
<p>(Nacional and Velez Sarsfield already qualified)</p>
<p>Group 3</p>
<p> Colo Colo (Chile)	     4  3  1  0  6  2  10</p>
<p> Universidad Catolica (Chile)6  2  2  2 15  6   8</p>
<p> Minerven (Venezuela)	  5  2  1  2  2  7   7</p>
<p> Mineros (Venezuela)	   5  0  2  3  1  9   2</p>
<p>(Colo Colo, Universidad Catolica and Minerven qualify)</p>
<p>Group 4</p>
<p> Gremio			    5  3  0  2  8  3   9</p>
<p> Sporting Cristal (Peru)     4  2  2  0  3  1   8</p>
<p> Cruzeiro (Brazil)	     5  2  0  3  4  4   6</p>
<p> Alianza			   6  1  2  3  2  9   5</p>
<p>(Gremio, Sporting Cristal and Cruzeiro qualify)</p>
<p>Group 5</p>
<p> Penarol (Uruguay)	     5  3  0  2  8  7   9</p>
<p> Millonarios (Colombia)	5  2  1  2  8  8   7</p>
<p> Deportivo Cali (Colombia)   3  1  1  1  5  4   4</p>
<p> Nacional (Uruguay)	    3  1  0  2  4  6   3</p>
<p>(Penarol already qualified)</p>
<p>Note: Top three teams in each group qualify for second round. Holders River Plate (Argentina) have a bye to the second round.</p>
